          },
          {
            "name": "fields",
            "type": "string",
            "required": false,
            "binding": "/query/fields",
            "description": "Comma-separated list of fields to return on each row. Fields you don't request are left out of the response instead of coming back as `null`, so a missing key means you didn't ask for it and `null` means the value is null. `id` is always included, whether or not you name it. Pass `all` to get every requestable field. An unknown field name returns `400` with the list of valid names and the closest match, so a typo is caught instead of being silently ignored. Requestable here: `applies_to_all_projects`, `applies_to_all_work_item_types`, `created_at`, `default_value`, `external_id`, `external_source`, `id`, `is_default`, `is_multi`, `is_required`, `issue_type_ids`, `name`, `options`, `project_ids`, `settings`, `sort_order`, `updated_at`, `updated_by_id`. See [Sparse fields](/api-reference/v2/sparse-fields)."
          },
